<urn:atm:triage:finding/CPR-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "CPR-001" ;
  triage:title "Stalled-task escalation is not terminal unless the team has exactly one lead" ;
  triage:description "Hostile closure review (general-purpose opus, task af4edaf6699568f49) @ 9f5aef2fe. Stalled-task escalation is not terminal unless the team has exactly one lead. Doc says: nudge-task-design.md §6 FIX: 'make the threshold TERMINAL, not multiplicative. At 10, escalate ONCE and STOP nudging.' Phase acceptance 2 claims this shipped. Code does: record_lead_audit is gated on `if let (Some(lead), Some(message_id)) = (outcome.lead, outcome.lead_write)`. `load_escalation_targets` computes `let lead = (leads.len() == 1).then(|| leads[0].clone())`, so zero leads AND two-or-more leads both yield None. record_lead_audit is the sole caller of record_lead_notified (crates/atm-storage-rusqlite/src/task_store.rs:344-364), the sole writer of lead_notified_count. dispose's Hold('stalled') arm keys only on lead_notified_count > 0, and escalate_stalled_task passes suppress_since: None so there is no mailbox suppression either. Recommendation: Make terminality independent of lead resolution: increment the stall counter (or record suppression) whenever EscalateStalled is dispatched, regardless of whether a lead was resolved or the write succeeded. Add tenth_reminder_escalates_once_then_silence variants for zero-lead and two-lead rosters before re-closing phase acceptance 2. fenix's ruling: make stall-escalation terminality independent of lead resolution -- audit fires on every EscalateStalled dispatch regardless of how many leads resolve (all-leads / recipients-only), not gated on a single-lead roster." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ba" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "correctness" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:source "qa" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "crates/atm-http-runtime/src/herdr_queue_wake_escalation.rs" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-12T07:08:18Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:deferredNote "fenix (ATM 01M2A8MZRBR51PDNSSS1HAV6NK, 2026-09-12T07:34:59Z): fixed at review-2 4079088f5 (all-leads TaskStalled mail, terminal stall audit on every dispatch, daemon fallback reference) plus e615755f7 (no-target fallback test); both gate-green." ;
  triage:foundIn triage:BA6 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-12T07:08:18Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/CPR-001/1> ;
